# Public entry point for the MCP servers on this host.
#
# Caddy terminates TLS (certificate from Let's Encrypt on the first request,
# renewed on its own) and forwards to the container over the shared `edge`
# network. It carries no secret of its own: each MCP server checks its own token,
# either from the Authorization header or from a `/t/<token>/…` URL prefix, so
# this file stays safe to read and to version.
#
# Access logging is deliberately left off (Caddy's default), because the URL of a
# connector request contains that token.
#
# One block per MCP server, one subdomain each. Adding the next one is three
# steps: an A record at the registrar, a block below with its own container name
# and port, then `docker compose exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile`
# — Caddy picks up the new host and fetches its certificate without dropping the
# running ones. No wildcard certificate: that would need a DNS-01 challenge
# against the registrar's API, which Strato does not offer.

{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

# project-pilot — the freelancermap worker
mcp.sequenz.io {
	reverse_proxy project-pilot-mcp:8765
}

